<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vietnamese Fatherland Front</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1955–present</span> · Also known as Vietnam Fatherland Front</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Vietnamese <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fatherland-front-bulgaria">Fatherland Front</a> is the umbrella organisation, led by the Communist Party, that groups <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>'s officially recognised mass organisations, such as the trade unions, the women's union and the youth union. Founded in North Vietnam in 1955, it absorbed the southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-liberation-front-south-yemen">National Liberation Front</a> in 1977. It vets and nominates the candidates for elections to the National Assembly and people's councils, ensuring that political life stays under party control.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vietnamese-fatherland-front.jpg" alt="Vietnamese Fatherland Front" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Trần Mai (original author), BCH Trung ương Mặt trận Tổ quốc Việt Nam (standardization) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bi%E1%BB%83u_tr%C6%B0ng_M%E1%BA%B7t_tr%E1%BA%ADn_T%E1%BB%95_qu%E1%BB%91c_Vi%E1%BB%87t_Nam.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
